WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:05.799
Adapting to sudden and unexpected changes
is a core tenet of human survival.

00:00:05.799 --> 00:00:10.340
However, abruptly finding yourself trapped
in an apparently infinite extradimensional

00:00:10.340 --> 00:00:15.350
pocket dimension in the form of a never-ending
Ikea… well, that can take a brief adjustment

00:00:15.350 --> 00:00:17.320
period to get used to.

00:00:17.320 --> 00:00:21.340
Callan hadn’t even noticed for the first
few moments, wandering through the aisles,

00:00:21.340 --> 00:00:26.770
aimlessly passing aisles of Hemnes and Trysils,
all the assembled display pieces of affordable

00:00:26.770 --> 00:00:28.289
flatpack furniture.

00:00:28.289 --> 00:00:32.140
It would have been more exciting, shopping
for all the accouterments for his brand new

00:00:32.140 --> 00:00:36.989
apartment, if Callan wasn’t being perpetually
reminded that he was moving in there on his

00:00:36.989 --> 00:00:37.989
own.

00:00:37.989 --> 00:00:41.479
It took him almost twenty minutes of walking
through the row of Ikea products for him to

00:00:41.479 --> 00:00:43.300
realize something felt off.

00:00:43.300 --> 00:00:45.690
He had hardly seen anybody else around.

00:00:45.690 --> 00:00:50.309
In fact, the more he thought about it, there
hadn’t even been any employees in their

00:00:50.309 --> 00:00:54.829
garish yellow polo shirts and blue pants at
the front of the store.

00:00:54.829 --> 00:00:59.180
Squinting off in the distance, Callan couldn’t
even see the far wall of the store.

00:00:59.180 --> 00:01:04.809
Sure, he knew Ikea outlets were big inside,
somewhere between a supermarket and an industrial

00:01:04.809 --> 00:01:08.100
warehouse, but this place seemed to go on
forever.

00:01:08.100 --> 00:01:12.630
Figuring that he had unknowingly stumbled
out of the store proper and into a large storage

00:01:12.630 --> 00:01:17.119
area, Callan turned around and started to
try retracing his steps back to the entrance.

00:01:17.119 --> 00:01:21.320
It was after another twenty minutes of taking
this approach that things went from feeling

00:01:21.320 --> 00:01:23.780
off to being overtly unsettling.

00:01:23.780 --> 00:01:28.789
By the time that over an hour had passed,
Callan was starting to panic, racing through

00:01:28.789 --> 00:01:33.930
the seemingly unending store, the rubber soles
of his sneakers squeaking against the epoxy

00:01:33.930 --> 00:01:39.080
resin floor as he yelled loudly for somebody,
anybody that might hear him.

00:01:39.080 --> 00:01:44.840
Before long, the latest victim to find themselves
lost inside SCP-3008 was hitting the first

00:01:44.840 --> 00:01:49.609
existential hurdle that came with being trapped
in the Infinite Ikea.

00:01:49.609 --> 00:01:55.329
Callan sat on a display couch – a two-seated
Söderhamn with a chaise longue, in case anyone

00:01:55.329 --> 00:01:56.329
was wondering.

00:01:56.329 --> 00:02:01.229
He was curled up into a ball, knees tucked
under his chin as he gently started rocking

00:02:01.229 --> 00:02:05.030
himself back and forth in a futile attempt
to comfort himself.

00:02:05.030 --> 00:02:10.090
It hadn’t yet quite sunk in just how trapped
he was, the thought that he might starve to

00:02:10.090 --> 00:02:13.380
death among the endless stock of Söres and
Fartygs.

00:02:13.380 --> 00:02:15.770
“The store is now closed.

00:02:15.770 --> 00:02:17.800
Please exit the building.”

00:02:17.800 --> 00:02:22.620
The sudden sound of a voice startled Callan,
snapping him out of his dread-filled daydream

00:02:22.620 --> 00:02:25.350
enough to realize the store now seemed darker.

00:02:25.350 --> 00:02:29.840
The lights had been gradually dimming the
longer he had stayed, creating an artificial

00:02:29.840 --> 00:02:31.880
night within SCP-3008.

00:02:31.880 --> 00:02:36.731
Normally the sign of another person after
being isolated would come as a relief, but

00:02:36.731 --> 00:02:39.240
whoever had spoken was nowhere to be seen.

00:02:39.240 --> 00:02:44.930
A slow, shuffling moved around the sofa Callan
was sitting on until he finally called out

00:02:44.930 --> 00:02:45.930
into the dark.

00:02:45.930 --> 00:02:46.930
“Hello?

00:02:46.930 --> 00:02:47.930
Is anyone there?”

00:02:47.930 --> 00:02:49.480
There was a pause.

00:02:49.480 --> 00:02:53.040
The movement stopped for an agonizingly quiet
moment.

00:02:53.040 --> 00:02:55.440
“The store is now closed.

00:02:55.440 --> 00:03:01.540
Please exit the building,” the voice repeated
as the unseen speaker stepped out of the shadows.

00:03:01.540 --> 00:03:04.680
Even in the low light, the creature was horrifying.

00:03:04.680 --> 00:03:06.900
Everything about it was just… wrong.

00:03:06.900 --> 00:03:10.910
For a split second, Callan thought it might
be an Ikea employee; it was wearing the uniform

00:03:10.910 --> 00:03:11.910
after all.

00:03:11.910 --> 00:03:17.710
But its bodily proportions were all off, arms
hanging nearly all the way down to the floor,

00:03:17.710 --> 00:03:20.450
hands and fingers enlarged and elongated.

00:03:20.450 --> 00:03:21.630
As for its face…

00:03:21.630 --> 00:03:23.370
it didn’t have one.

00:03:23.370 --> 00:03:25.580
The ordinary features were all missing.

00:03:25.580 --> 00:03:28.510
And now it was running right for him.

00:03:28.510 --> 00:03:31.010
Callan leaped over the back of the Söderhamn
and ran.

00:03:31.010 --> 00:03:34.070
His first instinct was to get away and hide.

00:03:34.070 --> 00:03:37.950
Checking over his shoulder, he caught sight
of the faceless creature dashing right past

00:03:37.950 --> 00:03:40.410
the couch with enough force to knock it over.

00:03:40.410 --> 00:03:44.370
In his startled state, looking out of the
corner of his eye at the encroaching Staff

00:03:44.370 --> 00:03:48.720
member, Callan tripped over his feet and tumbled
back down to the hard floor.

00:03:48.720 --> 00:03:51.970
The creature loomed over him as he tried to
crawl towards a nearby aisle.

00:03:51.970 --> 00:03:58.680
Looking up at it, the Staff member was reaching
for him, its big, disproportionate hand outstretched,

00:03:58.680 --> 00:04:01.740
trying to grab at Callan as he lay there helplessly.

00:04:01.740 --> 00:04:06.580
Suddenly, something struck the faceless creature;
someone barely visible in the dimmed lights

00:04:06.580 --> 00:04:11.470
of the store had leaped down from the shelves
of the aisle and swung a makeshift weapon

00:04:11.470 --> 00:04:12.910
at the Staff member.

00:04:12.910 --> 00:04:17.100
As it connected, the creature was reeled,
stumbling over itself, long enough for the

00:04:17.100 --> 00:04:19.430
mystery assailant to take another swipe at
it.

00:04:19.430 --> 00:04:23.500
Their weapon, comprised of what looked like
part of a curtain rail with a pair of kitchen

00:04:23.500 --> 00:04:29.190
knives at one end, impaled the Staff member,
ripping through its bright yellow Ikea polo

00:04:29.190 --> 00:04:31.350
and out the other side.

00:04:31.350 --> 00:04:35.190
Striding over to where Callan was still laying
on the floor, awestruck by the display he’d

00:04:35.190 --> 00:04:39.500
just witnessed, the figure pulled back the
hood of a rudimentary cloak they were wearing

00:04:39.500 --> 00:04:42.930
– fashioned by hand out of Aina curtain
fabric.

00:04:42.930 --> 00:04:47.370
Revealing herself with a stern, serious look
on her face, the woman reached a hand out

00:04:47.370 --> 00:04:52.870
to Callan, offering to help him up rather
than whatever that faceless creature had wanted

00:04:52.870 --> 00:04:53.870
with him.

00:04:53.870 --> 00:04:54.870
“It’s okay.

00:04:54.870 --> 00:04:57.721
I’m not going to hurt you,” she stated
as she pulled him back up to his feet.

00:04:57.721 --> 00:05:00.210
“This is probably all pretty confusing for
you, right?”

00:05:00.210 --> 00:05:02.340
Still too stunned to speak, Callan just nodded.

00:05:02.340 --> 00:05:04.880
“Yeah, it was for me too,” the woman replied.

00:05:04.880 --> 00:05:08.820
“We don’t have long until more Staff show
up, so you need to come with me and don’t

00:05:08.820 --> 00:05:09.840
ask questions, okay?”

00:05:09.840 --> 00:05:13.840
Seeing him nod again, she took Callan’s
hand and led him through the dark recesses

00:05:13.840 --> 00:05:15.510
of the Infinite Ikea.

00:05:15.510 --> 00:05:20.130
Stealthily, the pair of them snuck through
aisles, keeping low and ducking down out of

00:05:20.130 --> 00:05:24.560
sight whenever more of the Staff lumbered
into their path until they had wandered elsewhere,

00:05:24.560 --> 00:05:26.970
clearing the way for them to proceed.

00:05:26.970 --> 00:05:31.790
Callan’s new guide seemed to instinctively
know her way around the layout of the sprawling

00:05:31.790 --> 00:05:37.870
maze of flatpack Swedish furniture, quietly
urging him to stay close, offering him a hand

00:05:37.870 --> 00:05:40.730
up when they climbed up shelving units.

00:05:40.730 --> 00:05:43.990
Until finally, they arrived at their destination.

00:05:43.990 --> 00:05:48.580
A warm glow emanated from somewhere beyond
a tall, makeshift barrier.

00:05:48.580 --> 00:05:52.930
Sofas and cabinets were stacked on top of
each other, forming an intricate wall around

00:05:52.930 --> 00:05:55.490
an area of SCP-3008.

00:05:55.490 --> 00:06:00.139
And right in the middle of this rudimentary
barricade was a large, two-door Pax Fardal

00:06:00.139 --> 00:06:06.030
wardrobe, its back missing, doors inwards,
facing towards the inner side of the blockade.

00:06:06.030 --> 00:06:10.840
The guide stepped into the incomplete wardrobe
and gave a specifically timed knock, three

00:06:10.840 --> 00:06:15.060
beats with the third following the first two
after a short pause.

00:06:15.060 --> 00:06:19.680
From the other side, it sounded like something
was being hurriedly removed from the wardrobe’s

00:06:19.680 --> 00:06:23.889
handles, before the doors opened up to allow
her and Callan entry.

00:06:23.889 --> 00:06:27.930
Beyond the outer wall, this part of the Infinite
Ikea looked to have been converted into a

00:06:27.930 --> 00:06:33.200
small town, with a sign hanging above that
read ‘Decoration, Population: 58’.

00:06:33.200 --> 00:06:38.330
There were even more people within, most in
handmade clothing crafted out of scraps of

00:06:38.330 --> 00:06:42.900
fabric, along with the remnants of old clothes
from the outside world they’d been cut off

00:06:42.900 --> 00:06:43.900
from.

00:06:43.900 --> 00:06:47.600
Some looked like they were standing on guard,
carrying weapons similar to the guide’s

00:06:47.600 --> 00:06:52.520
weapon, others were sitting around together,
talking casually under the light of Sollefteå

00:06:52.520 --> 00:06:53.670
floor lamps.

00:06:53.670 --> 00:06:56.500
“Okay,” the guide sighed, turning back
to Callan.

00:06:56.500 --> 00:07:00.520
“We’re safe now that we’re inside the
wall so, you can talk again now.”

00:07:00.520 --> 00:07:03.680
“Uh, thank you,” he replied awkwardly.

00:07:03.680 --> 00:07:05.360
“For saving me, I mean.”

00:07:05.360 --> 00:07:08.020
“Don’t mention it,” she smiled for the
first time since they had met.

00:07:08.020 --> 00:07:10.780
“I’m sure you’ve got a lot of questions,
so ask away.

00:07:10.780 --> 00:07:12.790
I’ll do my best to answer as many as I can.”

00:07:12.790 --> 00:07:14.310
“Where am...”

00:07:14.310 --> 00:07:18.480
Callan’s voice trailed off, thinking of
a question he wanted to know the answer to

00:07:18.480 --> 00:07:21.850
even more than where he was or what was up
with this place.

00:07:21.850 --> 00:07:23.300
“Who are you?”

00:07:23.300 --> 00:07:26.170
The girl smiled and offered him an outstretched
hand.

00:07:26.170 --> 00:07:27.550
“My name’s Kiah.”

00:07:27.550 --> 00:07:31.389
Over the coming months, and with a lot of
direction from his new friend, Callan slowly

00:07:31.389 --> 00:07:35.490
started to adjust to living inside SCP-3008.

00:07:35.490 --> 00:07:39.570
The lifestyle was completely different from
what he was used to before; instead of renting

00:07:39.570 --> 00:07:44.640
or buying a house or apartment, the survivors
had established their own little settlements,

00:07:44.640 --> 00:07:49.440
using the copious amounts of Ikea furniture
around to construct homes for themselves.

00:07:49.440 --> 00:07:54.540
Without access to money – or any need for
it – nobody was self-serving either.

00:07:54.540 --> 00:07:58.420
Everyone chipped in and helped each other
out, agreed to take on tasks that would benefit

00:07:58.420 --> 00:07:59.800
their fellow survivors.

00:07:59.800 --> 00:08:02.910
There was a strong sense of community inside.

00:08:02.910 --> 00:08:05.850
All anyone had in the Infinite Ikea was each
other.

00:08:05.850 --> 00:08:11.389
They were all in the same situation, and surviving
it was made easier by cooperating.

00:08:11.389 --> 00:08:18.340
Kiah took responsibility for showing Callan
around, teaching him all about life in SCP-3008.

00:08:18.340 --> 00:08:22.840
When he asked her why she was so adamant about
keeping an eye on him, she replied by telling

00:08:22.840 --> 00:08:26.570
him that when she had arrived, she’d been
scared and alone.

00:08:26.570 --> 00:08:30.510
Even when the town of Decoration had taken
her in, Kiah still needed to learn all the

00:08:30.510 --> 00:08:32.090
basics on her own.

00:08:32.090 --> 00:08:35.610
She admitted that she had wished somebody
was there to teach her, and endeavored to

00:08:35.610 --> 00:08:37.999
do exactly that for Callan.

00:08:37.999 --> 00:08:42.229
She started by telling him what the best time
to head to the food court was.

00:08:42.229 --> 00:08:47.319
Every day, all the food in SCP-3008 would
somehow reappear, meaning that everyone could

00:08:47.319 --> 00:08:52.189
easily have their fill and survive without
having to hunt or kill each other in order

00:08:52.189 --> 00:08:53.189
to eat.

00:08:53.189 --> 00:08:57.149
Kiah’s next lesson involved teaching Callan
how to use Ikea stationery to leave subtle

00:08:57.149 --> 00:09:01.889
but recognizable symbols around the store,
so that if he was ever lost, he could find

00:09:01.889 --> 00:09:05.439
his way back to Decoration safely while avoiding
the Staff.

00:09:05.439 --> 00:09:08.220
“That’s the thing about living here,”
she said.

00:09:08.220 --> 00:09:11.319
“When we first arrive, we all think we’ve
got nothing.

00:09:11.319 --> 00:09:15.079
But this place has food, shelter, tools, everything
we need.

00:09:15.079 --> 00:09:17.319
We just have to learn to use what it gives
us.”

00:09:17.319 --> 00:09:20.820
As time went on, Callan found himself paired
up with Kiah for patrols.

00:09:20.820 --> 00:09:26.200
During the daytime, Staff would wander aimlessly
around the store, far more docile than they

00:09:26.200 --> 00:09:27.399
were at night.

00:09:27.399 --> 00:09:31.579
To make sure they were ready in the event
of an attack by the faceless creatures, the

00:09:31.579 --> 00:09:35.670
survivors mapped out the Staff’s movements,
reporting back to their settlements in case

00:09:35.670 --> 00:09:38.610
a large group of them were wandering too close.

00:09:38.610 --> 00:09:42.660
The more they went out together, the more
Callan found himself eagerly looking forward

00:09:42.660 --> 00:09:44.750
to being in Kiah’s company.

00:09:44.750 --> 00:09:49.379
Maybe it was just because she was the first
person he’d met inside the Infinite Ikea,

00:09:49.379 --> 00:09:53.660
perhaps because she had saved his life, but
there was something about her that made him

00:09:53.660 --> 00:09:56.069
feel a little less sad about being trapped
here.

00:09:56.069 --> 00:10:00.499
A feeling that would soon be cruelly ripped
away…

00:10:00.499 --> 00:10:02.610
It happened during an otherwise normal patrol.

00:10:02.610 --> 00:10:07.449
Kiah and Callan were checking the aisles,
keeping an eye on the Staff, and tallying

00:10:07.449 --> 00:10:09.119
every one they saw.

00:10:09.119 --> 00:10:13.329
The lights were starting to dim, indicating
it would soon be night again, and the pair

00:10:13.329 --> 00:10:16.130
of them agreed it was time to start heading
back to Decoration.

00:10:16.130 --> 00:10:20.350
That was until the sudden screeching caught
their attention.

00:10:20.350 --> 00:10:22.300
“What the hell was that?”

00:10:22.300 --> 00:10:23.300
Callan whispered.

00:10:23.300 --> 00:10:24.310
“No idea,” Kiah replied.

00:10:24.310 --> 00:10:26.209
“Could be someone else just arrived.”

00:10:26.209 --> 00:10:30.120
She gave a hand signal that instructed Callan
to split up; the pair of them moved through

00:10:30.120 --> 00:10:32.870
parallel aisles towards the source of the
noise.

00:10:32.870 --> 00:10:37.579
It sounded like stone scraping against the
floor, the weight of concrete causing whatever

00:10:37.579 --> 00:10:41.690
was being moved to generate a grating, eardrum
piercing racket.

00:10:41.690 --> 00:10:46.600
As he moved silently through the now familiar
space of SCP-3008, Callan wracked his brain

00:10:46.600 --> 00:10:49.350
about what could be making a noise like that.

00:10:49.350 --> 00:10:54.839
There was nothing that heavy or made of stone
within the Ikea, at least not that he had

00:10:54.839 --> 00:10:55.839
encountered.

00:10:55.839 --> 00:10:59.620
Even Kiah had looked surprised when first
detecting that sound; she’d been in here

00:10:59.620 --> 00:11:05.040
for so much longer, so it was telling when
even she had no clue what had made it.

00:11:05.040 --> 00:11:09.810
Suddenly, the noise stopped as quickly as
it had started, followed by the call of a

00:11:09.810 --> 00:11:11.170
familiar voice.

00:11:11.170 --> 00:11:12.639
“Callan, come look at this!”

00:11:12.639 --> 00:11:13.639
Kiah called.

00:11:13.639 --> 00:11:17.990
“What is it?” he shouted back, trying
to keep his voice low but audible, aware the

00:11:17.990 --> 00:11:19.110
Staff might be nearby.

00:11:19.110 --> 00:11:21.300
“I don’t know, some kind of statue.

00:11:21.300 --> 00:11:23.720
I’ve never seen anything like it in here
before-”

00:11:23.720 --> 00:11:29.420
Kiah was cut off mid-sentence, a quick, loud
scrape of concrete against the resin floor,

00:11:29.420 --> 00:11:31.779
followed by a blood-curdling scream.

00:11:31.779 --> 00:11:36.470
Eyes widening in horror, worried for her safety,
Callan sprinted further down the aisle, frantically

00:11:36.470 --> 00:11:38.060
calling Kiah’s name.

00:11:38.060 --> 00:11:40.670
As he reached the nearest corner, the scream
stopped.

00:11:40.670 --> 00:11:45.860
Her cries didn’t fade, lowering gradually
then petering off, instead her voice just

00:11:45.860 --> 00:11:50.920
cut out abruptly, with a sickening, muffled
crack like the sound of bone breaking beneath

00:11:50.920 --> 00:11:51.920
the skin.

00:11:51.920 --> 00:11:53.540
Panting, Callan whipped around the corner.

00:11:53.540 --> 00:11:58.790
That’s where he saw her, lying on the floor,
totally, unnervingly still.

00:11:58.790 --> 00:12:03.560
Her head was tilted at an unnatural angle,
the bones of her neck misaligned as blood

00:12:03.560 --> 00:12:05.050
dripped from her nose.

00:12:05.050 --> 00:12:09.700
Kiah’s body was lying at the feet of something
Callan had never seen since he’d arrived

00:12:09.700 --> 00:12:11.129
in the Infinite Ikea.

00:12:11.129 --> 00:12:16.899
It was some kind of sculpture, constructed
out of concrete over a metal rebar skeleton,

00:12:16.899 --> 00:12:20.660
with a crude attempt at spray painting over
its outer surface.

00:12:20.660 --> 00:12:27.399
He had no idea that this statue was often
referred to as SCP-173, otherwise known simply

00:12:27.399 --> 00:12:28.720
as the Sculpture.

00:12:28.720 --> 00:12:34.430
But then, Callan was more focused on how distraught
he felt at seeing Kiah dead on the floor.

00:12:34.430 --> 00:12:38.670
He had never worked up enough courage to tell
her, always worried that it would make things

00:12:38.670 --> 00:12:40.029
weird between them.

00:12:40.029 --> 00:12:44.699
And now he’d never get the chance again,
would never get to see her smile as he took

00:12:44.699 --> 00:12:49.470
on the lessons that she taught him about surviving
in SCP-3008.

00:12:49.470 --> 00:12:52.889
Feeling his eyes well up, Callan blinked away
tears.

00:12:52.889 --> 00:12:57.949
Suddenly, the Sculpture shot forward, in the
split second that his eyes were closed.

00:12:57.949 --> 00:13:01.860
Callan staggered away in shock and stumbled
over, landing on his back on the floor.

00:13:01.860 --> 00:13:07.300
As he went to get up, SCP-173 was inches away
from him, having moved yet again of its own

00:13:07.300 --> 00:13:08.300
accord.

00:13:08.300 --> 00:13:13.019
Carefully, Callan stood up, making sure to
keep looking straight at the sinister statue;

00:13:13.019 --> 00:13:19.089
it was getting clear what this thing was doing,
that it couldn’t move while being observed.

00:13:19.089 --> 00:13:26.199
Sure enough, as he started to cautiously back
away one step at a time, SCP-173 stayed still,

00:13:26.199 --> 00:13:27.959
frozen in place.

00:13:27.959 --> 00:13:32.619
Reaching the corner, his eyes stinging, desperate
to blink, Callan took a deep breath, fixing

00:13:32.619 --> 00:13:36.209
his gaze on the Sculpture for one moment longer
until…

00:13:36.209 --> 00:13:39.949
Turning and sprinting as fast as his legs
would allow, Callan had a few short moments

00:13:39.949 --> 00:13:43.490
to blink, sending his tears streaming down
his face.

00:13:43.490 --> 00:13:47.189
Behind him, he could hear the same oncoming
sound of concrete scraping heavily against

00:13:47.189 --> 00:13:49.939
the floor as the Sculpture gave chase.

00:13:49.939 --> 00:13:53.940
Callan rushed down the aisles, grabbing stacks
of flatpacks off the store shelves and pulling

00:13:53.940 --> 00:13:58.819
them to the floor, leaving piles upon piles
of mess behind him in a desperate attempt

00:13:58.819 --> 00:14:01.449
to slow the oncoming statue down.

00:14:01.449 --> 00:14:03.869
Why hadn’t it killed him already?

00:14:03.869 --> 00:14:05.709
Perhaps it was just playing with its food.

00:14:05.709 --> 00:14:10.320
He thought about trying to get back to Decoration,
wondering if maybe any of the other surviving

00:14:10.320 --> 00:14:14.220
settlers had encountered SCP-173 before.

00:14:14.220 --> 00:14:15.339
But as he ran.

00:14:15.339 --> 00:14:19.529
Callan caught sight of some of the symbols
he and Kiah had left around the store to help

00:14:19.529 --> 00:14:21.439
them find their way around.

00:14:21.439 --> 00:14:25.839
One of them denoted that there were hiding
spots nearby, and spurred him on to change

00:14:25.839 --> 00:14:27.549
course in that direction.

00:14:27.549 --> 00:14:31.549
He couldn’t lead the Sculpture back to the
town, not if it could slaughter them all in

00:14:31.549 --> 00:14:33.170
the blink of an eye.

00:14:33.170 --> 00:14:36.959
Finding a cramped cupboard, Callan climbed
inside and shut the door behind him.

00:14:36.959 --> 00:14:41.119
With his knees tucked under his chin, he couldn’t
help but remember the time he had arrived

00:14:41.119 --> 00:14:42.290
in the Infinite Ikea.

00:14:42.290 --> 00:14:46.850
He had done almost exactly the same thing
when he first encountered a Staff member;

00:14:46.850 --> 00:14:51.279
he’d run, and his first instinct had been
to just run away and hide.

00:14:51.279 --> 00:14:55.980
That was something about Kiah he had always
wished he could be, she was fearless, easily

00:14:55.980 --> 00:15:00.949
standing up to that Staff creature that would
have killed Callan if she hadn’t intervened.

00:15:00.949 --> 00:15:05.589
Trapped inside a cupboard, the deafening noise
of scraping concrete outside as the Sculpture

00:15:05.589 --> 00:15:09.079
searched for him, Callan felt like he’d
let her down.

00:15:09.079 --> 00:15:13.509
It seemed that, despite Kiah’s best efforts
to teach him, he was still scared.

00:15:13.509 --> 00:15:17.819
As he sat in the dark, praying the Sculpture
wouldn’t find him, he apologized under his

00:15:17.819 --> 00:15:18.930
breath to her.

00:15:18.930 --> 00:15:23.129
Callan started replaying every moment he and
Kiah had spent together, partly to keep her

00:15:23.129 --> 00:15:28.920
alive in his memory but also so that he could
at least think of something good before SCP-173

00:15:28.920 --> 00:15:32.329
found him and broke his neck the same way.

00:15:32.329 --> 00:15:37.949
Every lesson about life in SCP-3008, every
one of Kiah's skills she had painstakingly

00:15:37.949 --> 00:15:43.670
passed on were all still there, including
the best piece of advice she’d ever given.

00:15:43.670 --> 00:15:47.040
“We have to learn to use what this place
gives us.”

00:15:47.040 --> 00:15:51.649
Her words echoed in his head, as Callan finally
realized that she hadn’t just been talking

00:15:51.649 --> 00:15:56.949
about taking food from the food court or using
flatpacks to build shelters and settlements.

00:15:56.949 --> 00:16:01.959
She’d shown him how to navigate, how to
evade the Staff, and that everything in the

00:16:01.959 --> 00:16:06.299
Infinite Ikea could have some usefulness in
aiding survival.

00:16:06.299 --> 00:16:11.540
As much as it hurt knowing Kiah was gone,
Callan realized she might have already saved

00:16:11.540 --> 00:16:13.179
him a second time.

00:16:13.179 --> 00:16:19.149
He peeked out of the cupboard door; the Bathroom
section was just a quick dash away, and SCP-173

00:16:19.149 --> 00:16:20.569
was nowhere to be seen.

00:16:20.569 --> 00:16:26.350
A few moments later, the Sculpture detected
a loud sound; someone knocking things together,

00:16:26.350 --> 00:16:29.200
shouting, and whooping had caught its attention.

00:16:29.200 --> 00:16:33.449
Unobserved, the concrete creature zapped its
way towards the source of the commotion, moving

00:16:33.449 --> 00:16:37.089
quickly over towards the Bathroom department
of the store’s endless aisles.

00:16:37.089 --> 00:16:41.769
It came to a sudden, instinctive stop, sensing
eyes were watching it.

00:16:41.769 --> 00:16:46.059
Its entire stone body froze, rigidly fixed
to the spot it was standing on.

00:16:46.059 --> 00:16:50.679
It didn’t matter that the eyes watching
it this time were its own.

00:16:50.679 --> 00:16:56.749
Reflected back at itself in an assortment
of mirrors, SCP-173 was stuck.

00:16:56.749 --> 00:17:01.100
Someone had sprung a trap for the statue,
making it so that from the moment it shot

00:17:01.100 --> 00:17:04.760
over to its current position, it wouldn’t
be able to move.

00:17:04.760 --> 00:17:10.289
It was constantly being observed by itself,
no matter what angle its reflection would

00:17:10.289 --> 00:17:13.309
be within its own direct line of sight.

00:17:13.309 --> 00:17:18.070
Standing atop a nearby stack of shelves, Callan
looked down at the concrete statue, trapped

00:17:18.070 --> 00:17:21.500
in a collection of mirrors that he had assorted
into a ring.

00:17:21.500 --> 00:17:25.669
“Hey, you!” he called down at it, hoping
it could hear him even though it was frozen

00:17:25.669 --> 00:17:26.669
in place.

00:17:26.669 --> 00:17:29.830
“The store is now closed, please exit the
building!”

00:17:29.830 --> 00:17:34.260
He struck loudly against the metal frame of
the shelves, hoping it was loud enough to

00:17:34.260 --> 00:17:35.260
be heard.

00:17:35.260 --> 00:17:38.980
Sure enough, the Staff quickly descended on
the source of the noise.

00:17:38.980 --> 00:17:44.330
The night made the feral, hostile towards
anything they sensed to be an outside presence.

00:17:44.330 --> 00:17:50.929
They instantly honed in on SCP-173, attacking
it to little avail thanks to its stone body.

00:17:50.929 --> 00:17:55.529
Eventually, the group of Staff grew in number,
starting to heave the Sculpture as they went

00:17:55.529 --> 00:17:57.580
to remove it from the premises.

00:17:57.580 --> 00:18:03.190
Climbing from shelf to shelf, Callan followed
them the entire way; the Staff had no eyes,

00:18:03.190 --> 00:18:04.789
so technically couldn’t look at SCP-173.

00:18:04.789 --> 00:18:05.880
But he could.

00:18:05.880 --> 00:18:11.780
Even through tears, he didn’t blink until
the Sculpture had been removed.

00:18:11.780 --> 00:18:13.370
He wanted to make sure.

00:18:13.370 --> 00:18:15.160
It was what Kiah would have done.

00:18:15.160 --> 00:18:21.360
Now go check out “REAL IKEA MANAGER GOES
MAD WITH POWER IN SCP-3008” a and “SCP-096

00:18:21.360 --> 00:18:22.620
VS.

00:18:22.620 --> 00:18:26.549
SCP-173” for more videos featuring the anomalies
featured in today’s tale!

